<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Gwandu Emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">1808 CE – 1903 CE (approx.) · capital Gwandu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The western capital of the Sokoto Caliphate, ruled by the family of Abdullahi dan Fodio and overseeing the emirates of the west.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the victory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a> divided responsibility for his realm around 1812: his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-bello">Muhammad Bello</a> took the east from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto</a>, while his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullahi-dan-fodio">Abdullahi dan Fodio</a> took the west from Gwandu, a town he had fortified in 1808. Abdullahi, a respected scholar and poet, ruled until his death in 1829.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Gwandu ranked second to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto</a> and supervised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirates</a> such as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ilorin-emirate">Ilorin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nupe-kingdom">Nupe</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-liptako">Liptako</a> and the lands of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dendi-kingdom">Dendi kingdom</a>, receiving their tribute. Its rulers were scholars as well as administrators, and the emirate fought long wars with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kebbi">Kingdom of Kebbi</a>, who built the rival <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/argungu-emirate">Argungu Emirate</a>. Abdullahi's son Khalilu ruled from 1833 to 1858.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>British forces occupied Gwandu in 1903, and the Anglo-French boundary split its lands. The Nigerian part became an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/protectorate-of-northern-nigeria">Northern Nigeria</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> of Gwandu still reigns in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kebbi">Kebbi</a> State.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/gwandu-emirate.jpg" alt="Gwandu Emirate" width="320" height="199"><figcaption>Image: AbdurRahman AbdulMoneim · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sokoto_Sultanate_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1808 CE – 1903 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gwandu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abdullahi dan Fodio, Khalilu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Fulfulde, Hausa</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, <a href="/countries/niger">Niger</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Emirate of Gwandu, Gando</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1856&amp;focus=gwandu-emirate" aria-label="Gwandu Emirate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4808 1711 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Gwandu Emirate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5128 1967L5131 2028M5128 1967L5144 1947M5128 1967L5170 2068M5128 1967L5166 2094"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5131 2028h0M5144 1947h0M5170 2068h0M5166 2094h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5128 1967h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5128 1967h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Gwandu. <a href="/atlas?year=1856&amp;focus=gwandu-emirate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

